### ─── STEP 2: Seed Data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Run §1, §2, §3 in order to populate the three collections used by all
### subsequent examples. The laptops collection references memory and display
### collections via foreign keys — this enables the join examples below.

### §1. Seed the `memory` collection
### Each document describes a RAM module. Laptops reference these via `memory_id`.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "memory",
  "data": {
    "mem1": {
      "capacity_gb": 8,
      "type": "LPDDR5",
      "speed_mhz": 4266,
      "upgradeable": false
    },
    "mem2": {
      "capacity_gb": 16,
      "type": "LPDDR5",
      "speed_mhz": 4266,
      "upgradeable": false
    },
    "mem3": {
      "capacity_gb": 32,
      "type": "DDR5",
      "speed_mhz": 5600,
      "upgradeable": true
    },
    "mem4": {
      "capacity_gb": 64,
      "type": "DDR5",
      "speed_mhz": 5600,
      "upgradeable": true
    },
    "mem5": {
      "capacity_gb": 36,
      "type": "Unified",
      "speed_mhz": 6400,
      "upgradeable": false
    }
  }
}

